{
  "id": "COMPOUND:4709 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "XL999 is likely to interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through a pathway involving E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase UBR4. This is supported by the evidence that XL999 targets UBR4, which is subsequently targeted by Ulimorelin and Corticorelin ovine triflutate, both of which have a target of the gamma-2 subunit. The shared involvement of UBR4 in multiple pathways suggests a potential mechanism where XL999 may influence the ubiquitination or degradation of the gamma-2 subunit, thereby modulating its function. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent involvement of UBR4 across different ligands indicate a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of UBR4 as a central node in the regulation of the gamma-2 subunit, potentially through ubiquitination-dependent processes.",
